WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:07.080
I think most people understand that life is
special, but it’s not always clear what

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:13.580
makes life special and different from non-life
such as stars, planets and rocks.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:20.240
So we believe that what makes life so different
from these things is its persistence over

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.510
eons.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:27.730
For example, some of the genes that we carry,
written in our DNA, have been around for billions

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.869
of years — some of them almost unchanged.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:35.829
The way that is possible is because that information
and how to do certain things, how to build

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:37.990
these bodies, is written in an alphabet.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:43.280
This alphabet for DNA is known to be nucleic
acids, but we believe that that’s not a

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.590
universal property of all life.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.359
The only property that’s universal is the
fact that there is information written in

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:50.570
an alphabet.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:57.430
You can use alphabets from any kinds of different
chemicals and other planets somewhere in the

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:03.219
universe where there’s life, we might find
this same phenomenon of persistence, but written

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:09.280
with information in a different alphabet so
that the universality of life is its persistent

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.869
engendered by information encoded in an alphabet
that allows us to transmit the information

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:17.370
from generation to generation for eons to
come.

